"tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-ground the trip-risk rationale on the worst FULL-PHASE (setup+call+teardown) item time rather than the call-only 29.93 s figure, and state how the headroom invariant in test_timeout_budget_headroom.py remains meaningful once the budget covers setup/teardown (or note the two known ~120 s single-test items from bug 89d5 as the full-item worst case the 300 s budget must dwarf).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2333,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The 300 s budget is already sized to DWARF the slowest legitimate test (measured worst `call` 29.93 s, pinned in tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py), so charging fixture time to the first requesting test carries low trip risk.'","tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py:44-46 comment: 'These are `call` times, so `timeout_func_only = true` does not discount them' — the pinned 29.93 s figure is explicitly a body/call measurement, and its 2x-headroom invariant (_REQUIRED_HEADROOM) models a body-only budget.","Bug 89d5 comment records single-test durations of 124.0 s and 120.3 s that the old no-func_only --timeout=300 guard cleared — supporting safety, but confirming the relevant comparison is full-item, not the 29.93 s call figure.","Under pytest-timeout with func_only=False the timeout applies to the whole test item including fixture setup/teardown, so the sizing argument should compare 300 s against the worst FULL-PHASE item, not the worst call."],"finding":"The plan's low-trip-risk rationale is sized against a call-only worst time (29.93 s), but dropping func_only makes the 300 s budget govern the full per-item total (setup + call + teardown), with module/session-scoped fixture setup charged to the first requesting test — a different and larger basis than call alone.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe82f48015ebdb7e5","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section ('The 300 s budget is already sized to DWARF the slowest legitimate test (measured worst `call` 29.93 s ...)') and Scope bullet for tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py","norm_id":"n2ce124d5308619c4","priority":0.3667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A module- or session-scoped fixture whose setup runs long is charged entirely to the first test that requests it; that test's setup+call+teardown total, not its call time, is what the 300 s budget now bounds.","The headroom invariant in test_timeout_budget_headroom.py continues to assert budget >= 2 x (call-only worst) after the change, while the budget now covers a larger phase set — the invariant no longer models what it guards."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_pl